	\begin{center}
		{\Large \textbf{Ehresmann connections in a tangent category}}
		
		\vspace{4mm}
		{\large Geoffrey Cruttwell}
		
		\vspace{1mm}
		Mount Allison University, Canada
		
		\vspace{3mm}
		January 13th, 2026 — 16:00 (Europe/Lisbon) — Google Meet
	\end{center}
	
	\vspace{8mm}
	
	Tangent categories, first defined by Ji\v{r}\'{\i} Rosick\'y in 1984, are a categorical structure which allows one to abstractly work with and reason about many of the ideas in differential geometry. In this talk, I will discuss how to define and work with Ehresmann connections in a tangent category. No prior knowledge of tangent categories or differential geometry will be assumed.
	
	\vspace{4mm}
	
	The content of the talk is based on joint work with Marcello Lanfranchi.
	
